title: Speed-Dependent Headlamp Lighting (Town & Highway Beam Shaping)
raw_community_title: Speed-Dependent Lighting (SDL)
category: Lighting
platform: F-150 Lightning
model_years: 2022-2026
trim: Lariat / Platinum / Flash (Matrix LED Headlamps)
status: untested
source_sheet: Euro Kuga Mk3.5 / Ranger 6G / Mach-E GT Matrix LED Comparison & Livnitup Master Database
notes: |-
  UNTESTED / EXPERIMENTAL: Enables Speed-Dependent Light Mode (m2_SDL_Enable) in the Headlamp Control
  Module (HCM). Automatically widens and softens the low-beam light distribution at lower city/town speeds
  to better illuminate curbs, ditches, and pedestrians, and narrows/focuses the beam further down the road
  at highway speeds. Uses existing vehicle speed data on the CAN bus and does not require suspension ride-height sensors.

  NOTE ON HCM CRC BITS: The HCM requires secondary CRC calculation bits (in addition to the standard
  2-nibble checksum) and we do not currently have the offline calculation formula. Our working hypothesis
  is that setting the CRC bits to all 0s (0000) or all 1s (1111) and then, without resetting or power-cycling
  the module, immediately running the HCM headlamp calibration routine MIGHT trigger the module to generate
  the correct CRC bits internally.
steps:
- module: HCM
  address: 734-05-01
  notes: |-
    HCM requires CRC bits: try setting CRC bits to 0000 or 1111 and running the calibration routine
    without resetting the module to see if it generates valid CRC bits.
  targets:
  - mask: xxx* xxxx xx--
    community_hex: '1'
    type: discrete
    bits:
    - bit: 0
      action: 1
      feature_name: m2_SDL_Enable (SDLE)
      target_state: SDLE Enable
recipe_version: '1.1'
